WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.735
Look, here-- We're gonna--
We're having such a good time...

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.137
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-...but...

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.405
now you're going
to have to answer

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.240
for Sonny on the causeway. Okay.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.377
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-So, um...

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:13.445
I'm just saying
because to stand up--

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:17.349
you're one of 11 senators,
who voted not to certify

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.953
the last election, okay.
One of 11.

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:22.055
Do you think Biden didn't win?

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.023
Biden is clearly the president.

00:00:24.156 --> 00:00:26.025
Well, that's not the question
or the answer.

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.693
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.563
Do you think he won?
Was it a fair election?

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:32.298
Now, but those are
very different questions.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:33.866
-BILL MAHER: Okay--
-(STAMMERS)

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.668
Did he win
and is he the president?

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:36.870
Yes. Was it fair?

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.671
Look, there were lots of things
that were unfair

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:40.873
-about the last election.
-But it's been combed over more

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.710
than any election ever,
even by the people on your side,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.344
and they say it's not.
This is from your book.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.247
You say,
"Democrats whose capacity

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.816
for shamelessness never ceases
to astound me,

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:53.119
were no longer willing to play
by the rules of democracy."

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:55.688
Now, I know you're funny now,
but is that a joke?

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:56.923
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.558
The Democrats don't want
to play

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.493
-by the rules of democracy?
-What was the context

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.594
before and after that?
I'm sorry,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.062
the one sentence
I'm not remembering.

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:04.597
Well, that I know--
I don't know,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.598
but you wrote that.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.600
"The Democrats
are no longer willing

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.202
to play
by the rules of Democracy."

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:10.936
I wanted to read it
because I feel like,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.273
it's the exact opposite
of what I think,

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.842
which is that the Republicans,
including you,

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.478
January 6th etcetera,
are the ones who are no longer

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.280
willing to play
by the rules of Democracy.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.915
-It seems like--
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.050
Wait, wait--

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.520
It seems like your idea
has switched

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.388
in the Republican party to,

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.490
"elections only count
if we win,"

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:32.792
and then we will endlessly

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.427
litigate them,
even though your own--

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.363
It was laughed at a court,
like 60 different courts.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.499
I mean, all we have--
the-- the secretaries of state,

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.935
even the Republican ones,
everybody said you're--

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:46.372
Trump's own election,
people said it was the--

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:49.875
one of the most fair,
well-run elections ever.

00:01:50.075 --> 00:01:51.711
Why won't you let it go?

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.846
So, Bill, you're the one
that's not letting it go,

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.047
you're the one
that's asking about it.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.248
But-- but let me be clear
about something.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.083
I'm asking about your history
with it.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.019
Listen I believe passionately
in Democracy,

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:03.122
and-- and I also believe
voter fraud is a real,

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.658
and persistent problem,
and it's weird

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.059
that Democrats have taken
the view--

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.293
BILL: It's not.
It's been studied.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:09.595
Okay, so you don't think it is,
but you know what,

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:13.232
I have never once seen you
or any other host

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:16.268
ask Hillary Clinton
why she said in 2016

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.137
that Donald Trump
was an illegitimate president.

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:21.107
I've never seen
you ask Democrats

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.575
why they objected
to the presidential

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.278
certification in 2001,
that was George W. Bush

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.379
in 2005,
that was George W. Bush,

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:29.448
and in 2016,
that was Donald Trump.

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:31.150
And, so, I don't think we should
be--

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:32.852
have a double standard here.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:34.820
Okay, well,
there is a double standard,

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.255
'cause there's two different
things going on.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:39.025
One is a remonstration,
a mild protestation

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:43.328
of something-- They did--
Al Gore was the head

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:45.431
of the Senate at the time,
he had to pass the baton

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:47.066
in an election
he knew he won,

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:48.935
-and his--
-TED: He knew he won.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.269
-the other candidates--
-Are you an election denier?

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:51.704
You just said
Al Gore won that election.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:54.140
Well, he-- Okay, he did not win.
He won the-- I'm sorry,

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:55.808
you're right, you're right.
I meant to say he won

00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:57.042
the popular vote. Well--

00:02:57.142 --> 00:02:58.577
But-- but-- that's not
what chooses the president.

00:02:58.644 --> 00:02:59.545
Yes, I understand.
I understand.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.914
But the other candidate's
brother stopped the count.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:03.716
Okay, that's--
that is-- that's not accurate.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.784
The Supreme Court stopped
the count, his own brother

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:08.688
-ran that election in Florida--
-His brother was the governor

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.855
of Florida,
you know they counted--

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.624
Hold on, hold on a second.
I mean, facts matter.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.593
They counted the votes
four times in Florida.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.062
George W. Bush won
all four times,

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.197
I was part of the legal team
litigating that case,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.300
so I-- I was intimately
involved in Bush versus Gore.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.436
Every time they counted
the votes, Bush won.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:24.904
The bigger point
is that Al Gore

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:26.038
took one for the team.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.740
He came out and said,
"Okay, you know,

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:29.241
this was a really
fucked up election,

00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:31.143
but this is America."

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:34.614
The jewel in our crown
is that we pass power peacefully

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:35.948
and I'm not gonna be
the first guy

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.617
not to do that.
Nixon let it go in 1960,

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.087
that could have
been a-- screwy election,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.957
and Hillary came out
in her goddamn purple suit...

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:47.026
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-...so she did it

00:03:47.426 --> 00:03:49.062
before the sun rose.

00:03:49.628 --> 00:03:50.663
She did it before

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.397
the cock crowed three times.

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:54.867
She came out and said
"Trump is the president,"

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.136
that's what you guys
will not do.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.304
Joe Biden is the president,

00:03:58.437 --> 00:03:59.305
what do you mean
we won't do it?

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.774
I'm fighting him every day,
and he's screwing up the country

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:02.908
-and the world.
-(BILL LAUGHS)

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.044
So, I'm quite aware
Joe Biden's the president,

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:08.147
I wish he wasn't,
but it's not lost on me

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.017
who it is that caused a war
in Europe with Ukraine,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.653
that-- that gave
a hundred billion dollars

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.254
to Iran and the terrorists
attacking--

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:17.222
-He caused a war in Ukraine?
-Yes, you want to know how?

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.657
No, but next time.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.392
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)
-Thank you, Ted Cruz.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:22.462
All right, thank you,
that was spirited.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.196
-Come back and see us?
-I look forward to it.

00:04:24.329 --> 00:04:25.464
All right, I'll see you
on Overtime,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.333
we can finish it up. Ted Cruz.

